<title>USA: Putnam says names Jacobs to tax-exempt bond group.</title>
<headline>Putnam says names Jacobs to tax-exempt bond group.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boston-based Putnam Investments said Monday it named Jerome Jacobs a managing director and chief investment officer of the company's Tax-Exempt Bond Group.</p>
<p>Jacobs, who starts Oct 1, will report to William Curtin, managing director and chief investment officer of fixed income at Putnam.</p>
<p>Jacobs's unit manages about $18 billion in mutual fund and institutional assets, Putnam said.</p>
<p>Jacobs joined Putnam from the Vanguard Group, where he managed the tax-exempt bond group.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
